a hair or a tiny spot of blood, using this process. By using another process called \"neutron-activation analysis,\" a hair from the murder victim's head can show if he or she had been drugged or poisoned.\nThe biggest contribution to crime detection has been made by the computer. Suspects are found by the police quickly scanning large amounts of information.", "id": 3}, {"time": "66500", "image": "engenn8le03ob01re2img02.jpg", "text": "A criminal's car can also be identified by studying pieces of glass or paint found at the scene of the crime. The police still use Locard's idea of searching for clues, but today they can catch criminals by using these clues in much more efficient ways.", "id": 4}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}]}]}